### =============================================
### AGENT DEMO - Multi-Level Workflow Delegation
### =============================================
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates 4-level nested sub-workflows with cross-app delegation
### ARCHITECTURE:
###   Level 1: ProjectCoordinator (agent-coordinator) → CROSS-APP →
###   Level 2: Supervisor (agent-worker) → PARALLEL →
###   Level 3: Specialists (agent-worker) × N →
###   Level 4: AtomicTasks (agent-worker)
### KEY FEATURES:
###   - SubOrchestrationInstance with app_id parameter
###   - when_all for parallel specialist execution
###   - Rule-based task decomposition (no LLM)
###   - Failure injection at any level
### DURATION: Allow 5-10 minutes for full demonstration
###
### IMPORTANT: To use response variables:
###   1. Click "Send Request" on the POST request FIRST
###   2. Copy the project_id from the response
###   3. Use it in the GET request (or let the variable auto-populate)
### =============================================

### =============================================
### PHASE 1: SYSTEM PREPARATION
### =============================================

### 1. Health check for agent-coordinator service
GET http://localhost:3011/healthz

### 2. Health check for agent-worker service
GET http://localhost:3012/healthz

### 3. Restock inventory (optional - if testing with inventory)
POST http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory/restock

### =============================================
### PHASE 2: SIMPLE PROJECT (2 Tasks)
### =============================================

### 4. Submit a simple project with 2 tasks
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates minimal 4-level workflow hierarchy
### HIERARCHY:
###   - project_xxx (L1: Coordinator)
###     - project_xxx_supervisor (L2: Supervisor)
###       - project_xxx_specialist_0 (L3: Researcher)
###         - project_xxx_specialist_0_atomic (L4: Atomic)
###       - project_xxx_specialist_1 (L3: Analyst)
###         - project_xxx_specialist_1_atomic (L4: Atomic)
// @name simple_project
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Simple Report",
    "description": "Create a basic analysis report",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "task_count": 2,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 500
}

### 5. Check simple project status
### NOTE: Run the POST above first, then use the project_id from the response
### Option A: Use auto-captured variable (after running POST above)
@simple_project_id = {{simple_project.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{simple_project_id}}

### Option B: Manual - paste your project_id here
# GET http://localhost:3011/projects/project_xxxxxx

### =============================================
### PHASE 3: MODERATE PROJECT (3 Tasks)
### =============================================

### 6. Submit a moderate project with 3 tasks
### PURPOSE: Shows research -> analysis -> synthesis pipeline
### EXPECTED: 3 specialists run in parallel
// @name moderate_project
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Market Analysis",
    "description": "Conduct comprehensive market research and analysis",
    "complexity": "moderate",
    "task_count": 3,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 400
}

### 7. Check moderate project status
### NOTE: Run the POST above first, then use the project_id from the response
@moderate_project_id = {{moderate_project.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{moderate_project_id}}

### Option B: Manual - paste your project_id here
# GET http://localhost:3011/projects/project_xxxxxx

### =============================================
### PHASE 4: COMPLEX PROJECT (4 Tasks)
### =============================================

### 8. Submit a complex project with 4 tasks
### PURPOSE: Full pipeline - research -> analysis -> synthesis -> validation
### DEMONSTRATES: Maximum parallelism with 4 specialists
// @name complex_project
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Strategic Initiative",
    "description": "Full strategic analysis with validation",
    "complexity": "complex",
    "task_count": 4,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 300
}

### 9. Check complex project status
@complex_project_id = {{complex_project.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{complex_project_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 5: FAILURE INJECTION - Level 1
### =============================================

### 10. Submit project with failure at Level 1 (Coordinator)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates failure at the entry point
### EXPECTED: Immediate failure, no delegation to supervisor
// @name fail_level_1
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Fail at Coordinator",
    "description": "Test Level 1 failure injection",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "task_count": 2,
    "fail_at_level": 1,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 300
}

### 11. Check Level 1 failure status
@fail_level_1_id = {{fail_level_1.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{fail_level_1_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 6: FAILURE INJECTION - Level 2
### =============================================

### 12. Submit project with failure at Level 2 (Supervisor)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates failure after cross-app delegation
### EXPECTED: Coordinator succeeds, supervisor fails before spawning specialists
// @name fail_level_2
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Fail at Supervisor",
    "description": "Test Level 2 failure injection",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "task_count": 2,
    "fail_at_level": 2,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 300
}

### 13. Check Level 2 failure status
@fail_level_2_id = {{fail_level_2.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{fail_level_2_id}}

### =============================================
