{
    "name": "Fail at Specialist",
    "description": "Test Level 3 failure injection",
    "complexity": "moderate",
    "task_count": 3,
    "fail_at_level": 3,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 300
}

### 15. Check Level 3 failure status
@fail_level_3_id = {{fail_level_3.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{fail_level_3_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 8: FAILURE INJECTION - Level 4
### =============================================

### 16. Submit project with failure at Level 4 (Atomic Task)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates failure at the deepest level
### EXPECTED: Atomic tasks fail, bubbles up through specialists
// @name fail_level_4
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Fail at Atomic Task",
    "description": "Test Level 4 failure injection",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "task_count": 2,
    "fail_at_level": 4,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 300
}

### 17. Check Level 4 failure status
@fail_level_4_id = {{fail_level_4.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{fail_level_4_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 9: QUICK EXECUTION (Minimal Delays)
### =============================================

### 18. Submit fast project for quick demo
### PURPOSE: Rapid execution for live demos
### EXPECTED: All 4 levels complete quickly
// @name quick_project
POST http://localhost:3011/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Quick Demo",
    "description": "Fast execution demonstration",
    "complexity": "simple",
    "task_count": 2,
    "simulate_delay_ms": 100
}

### 19. Check quick project status
@quick_project_id = {{quick_project.response.body.project_id}}

GET http://localhost:3011/projects/{{quick_project_id}}

### =============================================
### DEMONSTRATION POINTS
### =============================================
###
### KEY FEATURES TO HIGHLIGHT:
###
### 1. CROSS-APP WORKFLOW DELEGATION:
###    - agent-coordinator calls agent-worker via app_id
###    - SubOrchestrationInstanceCreated event shows cross-app call
###    - Instance IDs maintain correlation across services
###
### 2. 4-LEVEL WORKFLOW HIERARCHY:
###    - L1-COORDINATOR: Entry point, task decomposition
###    - L2-SUPERVISOR: Parallel specialist management
###    - L3-SPECIALIST: Role-based task processing
###    - L4-ATOMIC: Timer-based task execution
###
### 3. PARALLEL EXECUTION:
###    - Supervisor uses when_all for parallel specialists
###    - All specialists run concurrently
###    - Results aggregated after completion
###
### 4. RULE-BASED AGENT LOGIC:
###    - No LLM required - deterministic rules
###    - Complexity maps to task count
###    - Task types map to specialist roles
###
### 5. FAILURE INJECTION:
###    - fail_at_level: 1-4 controls failure point
###    - Useful for testing error handling
###    - Shows error propagation through levels
###
### 6. NOTIFICATION PREFIXES:
###    - [L1-COORDINATOR] - Level 1 events
###    - [L2-SUPERVISOR] - Level 2 events
###    - [L3-SPECIALIST:ROLE] - Level 3 events
###    - [L4-ATOMIC] - Level 4 events
###
### =============================================
### CATALYST UI VERIFICATION:
###
### 1. Open Catalyst UI at console.diagrid.io
### 2. Navigate to Workflows section
### 3. Watch for these workflow patterns:
###    - project_xxx (parent)
###    - project_xxx_supervisor (child, cross-app)
###    - project_xxx_specialist_0..N (grandchildren)
###    - project_xxx_specialist_0_atomic (great-grandchildren)
###
### 4. Verify SubOrchestrationInstance events show:
###    - instance_id with proper nesting
###    - app_id="agent-worker" for cross-app calls
###
### =============================================
### DEMO EXECUTION GUIDE:
###
### PREPARATION:
###   1. Start all services: diagrid dev run -f dapr.yaml
###   2. Open notifications UI at localhost:8080
###   3. Open Catalyst UI for workflow visualization
###
### SUGGESTED FLOW:
###   1. Start with simple project (Phase 2)
###   2. Show parallel execution with moderate (Phase 3)
###   3. Demonstrate full pipeline with complex (Phase 4)
###   4. Show failure handling (Phases 5-8)
###   5. Quick demo for rapid iteration (Phase 9)
###
### EXPECTED DURATION: 5-10 minutes
### NOTIFICATION RATE: 10-30 events per project
### =============================================
